a new hotel development is in the works  for downtown henderson and the owner of  the pass casino is hoping to put this  new hotel right next to a casino which  is over on water street and atlantic way  mary jane bellies is sharing the plans  and what it will bring to the water  street district  a new hotel could soon take over part of  the parking lot at the pass casino in  henderson joseph d simone the owner of  the pass says the project is currently  in the administrative design review  stage and is working with hotel brand  ihg to create the second atwell suites  in the country there'll be a wine bar in  front by the water street  and there'll be a two two story lounge  area  in the front of the hotel building  there will be 90 rooms most of them  suites  it will accommodate the the hockey arena  and the families that go there it will  accommodate all the incredible amount of  traffic water street gets especially  during the weekends desimone says  building a hotel has always been top of  mind not just to complement the past  casino but a growing area too he is now  preparing to submit the plans to the  city of henderson for approval for  pacific diner owner marvin wallace new  growth means more customers  areas  growing pretty much every week every  month every day  i mean we've had lots of restaurants  come in lots of bars come in it's great  it's all helping the area grow and  become a lot more popular redevelopment  manager anthony malloy with the city of  henderson says they are excited to  welcome the new hotel as it'll help  house tourists and bring in foot traffic  i think that many people haven't been to  water street in a long time maybe even a  decade and so what they can expect is  really to see a transformation from what  they had previously  seen and experienced to what it is today  reporting from water street and atlantic  avenue mary jane balleza live local now
 

